in python, do not use threading inside async def, use asyncio.create_task to run block function inside async def and it will not block rest code

1. do not use threading inside async def
2. use asyncio.create_task to run another async function without await inside async def, and it will not block rest code
3. use loop.run_in_executor to run blocking function inside async def

`await` will yield control to event loop, other function inside event loop will run, but the `await` will block the rest code
until it get result

1. loop.run_in_executor() WITHOUT await - It WILL run immediately! return Future object, not block rest code
2. await loop.run_in_executor() - Runs AND returns the actual result (not a Future), block rest code
3. asyncio.create_task() WITHOUT await - Starts immediately, returns a Task object, not block rest code
4. await asyncio.create_task() - Starts immediately AND awaits the result, block rest code
